      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Run and debrief the trial close using the new checklist.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 523876,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, I've completed the trial run of the new close process on last month's data, as per T10. Overall, it went smoothly and we were faster. The main issue was a bottleneck on Day 3 around collecting supporting documents for accruals, which delayed subsequent steps. The timings are logged in the test version of A1.",
            "mentions": [
              81248,
              16157,
              375245,
              457591
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10",
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 375245,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Yeah, that part was slow for me too. I also had trouble finding the right certificate for one of the revenue entries. It took a while to track down.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 457591,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Thanks for running this. For the Day 3 bottleneck, could we move the 'Send final reminder for supporting docs' task from Day 2 to Day 1? That gives departments an extra day and might smooth out the collection process. We could also start the preliminary review of submitted docs in parallel on Day 2.",
            "mentions": [
              523876
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 81248,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "That's a good idea. Shifting that reminder earlier makes sense. What does everyone else think?",
            "mentions": [
              16157,
              375245,
              523876
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 523876,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "I agree, that would definitely help. It gives us more time to chase any missing items before the deadline.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 16157,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "During the compliance review step (T12), did we log the specific missing certificates in the findings log A8? To prevent the issue @375245 mentioned, we could add a mandatory 'pre-review check' to A1 on Day 4, where the entry preparer confirms all attachments are present before passing it for final review. This makes the process more robust.",
